    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md`, Family D). Consolidates F36.D2 + F40.B5 (5 additional shapes) previously folded onto INV-zurih. Full evidence remains on INV-zurih's pass-36 and pass-40 discussion entries; this row provides discrete representation.\n\nThe audit's verdict: F36.D2 / F40.B5 are structurally distinct from INV-zurih's generic \"missing CLI exception handler\" scope. INV-zurih is about catching tracebacks AT the CLI layer; this row is about input-shape validation BEFORE the parser fans out. Different fix-site (`load_claims` body vs CLI exception wrapper), different downstream behavior (clear \"expected shape X\" message vs friendly traceback).\n\n## Symptom\n\n`verify-claims --claims <file>` accepts a YAML file. `load_claims` at `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/verify_claims.py:201` presumes the YAML root is a dict containing `claims:` and calls `data.get('claims', [])` without a type or null check. Six distinct unhandled YAML shapes traceback at this line.\n\n**Pass-36 F36.D2 (initial finding — list-root case).** `yaml.safe_load()` returns whatever the YAML root is. A bare top-level list of claim records (without `claims:` key) crashes with:\n```\nAttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'get'\n  at verify_claims.py:201 in load_claims:\n    for entry in data.get('claims', []):\n                  ^^^^^^^^\n```\n\n**Pass-40 F40.B5 (5 additional shapes).** Full 9-shape matrix:\n\n| Shape | rc | tb | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| missing path | 1 | 0 | clean \"Claims file not found\" |\n| empty YAML | 0 | 0 | \"No claims found in file\" |\n| **scalar** (`hello`) | 1 | **1** | AttributeError: str has no .get |\n| **claims: null** | 1 | **1** | TypeError: NoneType not iterable |\n| **claims: ~** | 1 | **1** | same TypeError |\n| **binary file** | 1 | **1** | yaml.reader.ReaderError leaks 5 layers deep |\n| **directory path** | 1 | **1** | IsADirectoryError from open() |\n| list-root (F36.D2) | 1 | **1** | AttributeError |\n| claims: [] | 0 | 0 | clean \"No claims found\" |\n| empty_dict {} | 0 | 0 | clean \"No claims found\" |\n\n**Six** distinct unhandled-traceback shapes across the matrix. Notable asymmetry: `claims: []` and `{}` give clean rc=0 \"No claims found\" but their semantic siblings `claims: null` and `claims: ~` traceback. All four are reasonable YAML representations of \"no claims\" but only 2 are handled.\n\n## Invariant\n\n`verify-claims --claims <file>` must validate the parsed YAML's shape against the expected schema (`{claims: [list of claim records]}`) at load time and emit a clear rc=2 + `\"Error: expected top-level 'claims:' key with a list value (got <observed shape>)\"` for any deviation. Six specific failure shapes to handle:\n\n1. scalar YAML root (string, number, bool)\n2. list YAML root (no top-level `claims:` key)\n3. `claims: null` / `claims: ~`\n4. `claims: <scalar>` (non-list value)\n5. binary file (catch `yaml.reader.ReaderError` and surface friendly error)\n6. directory path (check `os.path.isdir` before open)\n\nEmpty file, empty dict `{}`, and `claims: []` correctly produce rc=0 \"No claims found\" and should continue to do so.\n\nCousin invariant: `verify-claims --help` should document the expected YAML shape. Currently the format is undocumented — F36.D2 explicitly notes \"accepted formats are undocumented, and one of them silently crashes.\"\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nSingle fix-site at `verify_claims.py:200-201` plus the `open()` and `yaml.safe_load()` wrappers:\n\n```python\n# pre-checks\nif os.path.isdir(path):\n    raise CLIError(f\"Error: claims path is a directory: {path}\")\ntry:\n    with open(path, 'rb') as fh:\n        raw = fh.read()\nexcept yaml.reader.ReaderError:\n    raise CLIError(f\"Error: file is not valid YAML/text: {path}\")\ndata = yaml.safe_load(raw) if raw.strip() else {}\n\n# shape check\nif not isinstance(data, dict):\n    raise CLIError(\n        f\"Error: expected top-level dict with 'claims:' key, got {type(data).__name__}\"\n    )\nclaims_list = data.get('claims', [])\nif claims_list is None:\n    claims_list = []\nif not isinstance(claims_list, list):\n    raise CLIError(\n        f\"Error: 'claims:' must be a list, got {type(claims_list).__name__}\"\n    )\n```\n\nPlus a `--help` documentation update on the expected shape (which Family E entries also touch — see WI-search-case-sensitivity-split for the pattern).\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F36.D2** — INV-zurih discussion entry 2026-06-02T18:XX (pass-36 batch; see paragraph beginning \"F36.D2 (NEW BUG): verify-claims --claims accepts EITHER top-level list YAML or dict-with-claims-key YAML\").\n- **F40.B5** — INV-zurih discussion entry 2026-06-03T00:12:41 (pass-40 batch; full 9-shape matrix; paragraph beginning \"Pass-40 F40.B5 — verify-claims --claims 9-shape matrix\").\n\nLab notebooks: passes 36, 40 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **WI-himas** (META: Add top-level CLI exception handler) — umbrella for CLI input-boundary failure modes.\n- Sibling: **INV-zurih** (verify-claims unhandled traceback on malformed YAML — same subcommand, broader scope at the CLI exception-handler layer; this row is the input-shape-validation pre-check).\n- Sibling: **WI-read-subcmd-schema-validate** (Family D — analogous input-shape gap on the read subcommands).\n- Sibling: **INV-sozop** (read subcommands traceback on malformed --input — sibling input-shape failure mode at a different boundary)."  # 80bf
